<title>USA: PP&amp;L Susquehanna 2 at 75 pct power - NRC.</title>
<headline>PP&amp;L Susquehanna 2 at 75 pct power - NRC.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pennsylvania Power and Light Co's 1,094 megawatt (MW) Susquehanna 2 nuclear power unit has been reduced to 75 percent power for a condenser leak, Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said Friday.</p>
<p>The unit, in Berwick, Pa., was operating at full power Thursday.</p>
<p>The adjacent unit 1, with a generating capacity of 1,090 MW, is operating at 100 percent power, the NRC said in its morning plant status report.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
</text>
